  "interpretation_notes": [
    "Units follow CSV headers: capacity and volumetric throughput in thousand cubic metres per day; energy throughput in gigajoules per day.",
    "The gas dictionary capacity description says gigajoules per day while its column header says 1000 m3/d. Preserve this source metadata inconsistency; never mix the energy and volume columns.",
    "Brunswick is an observed monthly series although the gas family is described generally as daily. It must not be counted as daily completeness or summed as daily volume without a documented monthly-average assumption.",
    "Values at successive or interconnected points can represent the same gas; arbitrary sums across key points are not Canadian production or unique physical throughput.",
    "CER explains reported capacity can be an estimate; throughput above that estimate does not establish a safety or regulatory breach.",
    "Current legal-entity labels in throughput data differ from historical incident labels. No incident-to-key-point relationship is inferred from company names."
  ]
